{"reference":"John 17","book":"John","chapter":17,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Prayer’s Unity","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One interpretive reading understands this prayer as holding together Jesus’ glorification, the protection and sanctification of his followers in truth, their mission, and their unity. In that reading, the unity described in the chapter is modeled on the relation of Father and Son and should not be taken to require enforced institutional conformity or the concealment of abuse.","verse_refs":["John 17:1-26"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_john_017_53d3df456692d068624c3622"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}